  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Derrisin and Peptide deformylase, mediated through the Taste receptor type 2 member 31. This pathway is supported by multiple high-scoring connections, with Derrisin acting as a target for three distinct entities—Taste receptor type 2 member 31, Sugiol, and Npc158230—all of which are targets of Peptide deformylase. The shared involvement of Peptide deformylase as a target across these pathways indicates a possible functional link, though the exact mechanism by which Derrisin influences these targets remains unclear. The presence of multiple independent pathways pointing to Peptide deformylase suggests that Derrisin may modulate the activity of these receptors, potentially through a common downstream effect. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that Derrisin could interact with Peptide deformylase in a biological context, though further experimental validation is needed to establish the precise nature of this interaction.",
